ASIX USB NIC driver v4.2.100 Beta1
==================================

This directory contains the ASIX v4.2.100 Beta1 driver integrated into the kernel
tree.  It is built by CONFIG_USB_NET_AX88179_178A and produces ax_usb_nic.
The in-kernel ax88179_178a object is intentionally not built at the same time.

Supported ASIX revisions sharing USB product ID 0x1790 are selected by
bcdDevice:

  0x0100  AX88179
  0x0200  AX88179A/AX88179B
  0x0300  AX88772D/AX88772E
  0x0400  AX88279
  0x0500  AX88279A

The driver also supports AX88178A and the compatible OEM IDs listed in
ax_main.c.  Devices exposing CDC ECM/NCM and vendor configurations are moved
to the vendor configuration by the driver; no udev rule or module blacklist
is required for this in-tree integration.

Configuration
-------------

Feature options are available below CONFIG_USB_NET_AX88179_178A.  The default
configuration enables aggressive interrupt handling, large send offload, USB
link power management, and the low-power suspend sequence.  PTP and other
special-purpose test or queue features are disabled by default.

The autodetach module parameter has these values when autodetach support is
compiled in:

  -1  use the compiled default (enabled)
   0  disable autodetach
   1  enable autodetach

Programming and IEEE test tools
-------------------------------

The programmer, IEEE test, and axcmd sources are retained for factory and
diagnostic use, but are not part of the kernel build.  Build them explicitly
with the target userspace compiler when needed:

  cc -Werror ax88179_programmer.c -o ax88179_programmer
  cc -Werror ax88179a_programmer.c \
     -o ax88179b_179a_772e_772d_programmer
  cc -Werror ax88279_programmer.c -o ax88279a_279_programmer
  cc -Werror ax88179a_ieee.c -o ax88279_179ab_772e_ieee
  cc -Werror axcmd.c -o axcmd

Private programming commands require CONFIG_USB_AX_USB_NIC_IOCTL_DEBUG.
PTP requires CONFIG_USB_AX_USB_NIC_PTP and CONFIG_PTP_1588_CLOCK.
